{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Let there be luminaries, etc.</b> From the first day they were created, and on the fourth day He commanded them to be suspended in the firmament. And likewise all products of heaven and earth were created from the first day, and each and every one was fixed on the day decreed upon it. That is what is written: אֵת הַשָּׁמַיִם — to include their products; וְאֵת הָאָרֶץ — to include its products." "<b>Let there be luminaries.</b> It is written deficient — without a vav — because it is a day of cursing, that croup should fall upon infants. That is what we learned: on four [fasts] they would fast over croup that it should not fall upon infants." "<b>To distinguish between the day and between the night.</b> From when the first light was stored away. But during the seven days of Genesis the first light and the first darkness served together, both by day and by night." "<b>And for signs.</b> When the luminaries are eclipsed, it is a bad sign for the world, as was said: מֵאֹתוֹת הַשָּׁמַיִם אַל תֵּחָתּוּ (Jeremiah 10). When you do the will of the Holy One, blessed be He, you need not fear the punishment." "<b>And for seasons.</b> On account of the future — for Israel are destined to be commanded concerning the festivals, and they are reckoned by the birth of the moon." "<b>And for days.</b> The sun's use is half a day and the moon's use is its half — behold, a full day." "<b>And years.</b> At the end of 365 days (MS: and a fourth of a day), they complete their course through the twelve signs of the zodiac that serve them — and that is a year, and they return and begin a second time to revolve in the sphere in their first course."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:13.031745574Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}